OL,3,GNEWSABoy with rare condition being
OL,4,Ahelped by horses
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mum on the Isle of Man has praised a
OL,7,Flocal horse-riding charity after seeing
OL,8,Fher 11-year-old with a rare genetic
OL,9,Fcondition, come home happier, chattier
OL,10,Fand more confident after each session.
OL,12,FMargaret's son Donnchadh, who has
OL,13,FKibuki syndrome, has been going to
OL,14,FRiding for the Disabled classes for
OL,15,Ffour years.
OL,17,FThe condition affects about one in
OL,18,Fevery 32,000 people, and Margaret
OL,19,Fbelieves he is the only one with it on
OL,20,Fthe island.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB IOM NewsC Reg TVF Clean Feed
